## Current project status

Sugam is a Phase 1 local Android application.

Technology stack:

* Kotlin
* Jetpack Compose
* Material 3
* MVVM
* Room / SQLite
* Kotlin Coroutines
* StateFlow / Flow
* Navigation Compose
* Gradle / Kotlin DSL

The application is successfully running on a physical Android device.

Current Room database version is **3**.

Architecture:

```text
Compose UI
    ↓
ViewModel
    ↓
Repository
    ↓
Room
    ↓
SQLite
```

Important architectural rules:

* UI must not access Room directly.
* Repository is the persistence boundary.
* Appointments reference `physioId`, not a physio name.
* Multiple physios must be supported.
* Historical appointments must remain valid even if a physio is deactivated.
* Double-booking prevention must not depend only on UI validation.
* Phase 1 remains local-only.
* Do not introduce cloud/backend functionality.

